  "body": "**Research consolidation (no \u03ba claim).** The T74 line has fifteen open conditional-\u03ba PRs, and their descriptions and READMEs contain many interlocking \"exceeds PR#### by X\" and \"PR#### (kappa X)\" statements. This package:\n- pins each PR's own claim file (16 pinned, counting the PR2265 baseline);\n- recomputes every numeric statement between pinned PRs that it transcribed from PR bodies and pinned READMEs, with exact rational arithmetic;\n- parses the predecessor gates in each pinned `verify_release.py`;\n- maps which claims have independent checks.\n\n### Findings\n- **The release gates are right, so none of the errors below affects any \u03ba value or release gate.** 82 predecessor gates are attributed to pinned PRs and all pass:\n  - 55 are EXACT;\n  - 17 are conservative (literal above the named \u03ba);\n  - 10 sit below the named \u03ba. All 10 are PR2265's published 43-digit \u03ba, a truncation 9.7e-45 below its pinned value, which is immaterial against margins of at least 1.28e-5.\n- **95 stated numbers checked (32 from bodies, 63 from READMEs): 84 consistent, 11 flagged.**\n  - **(A) Wrong target.** Each printed number is the difference to a different PR than the one named:\n    - #2302 body: \"\u2026 PR2269 by 8.48163E-8\" is the difference to PR2288; the difference to PR2269 is 1.48628E-7.\n    - #2374 body and README: \"\u2026 PR2312 by 1.28957E-7\" is the difference to PR2349; the difference to PR2312 is 3.03884E-7.\n    - #2435 body and README: \"\u2026 PR2312 by 1.31639E-6\" is the difference to PR2374; the difference to PR2312 is 1.62028E-6.\n  - **(B) Own \u03ba quoted as the predecessor's.** The READMEs of #2435, #2447 and #2474 each say \"exceeds PR#### (our previous package, kappa X\u2026)\" with X equal to the package's own \u03ba.\n  - **(C) Stale copied boilerplate.** The #2288, #2302 and #2312 READMEs repeat PR2269's \"exceeds PR2265 by about 1.28e-5\". The true values are 1.290e-5, 1.298e-5 and 1.348e-5.\n- **One gate label slip.** In five scripts, a gate whose comment and literal are PR2363's \u03ba reports \"does not exceed PR2322\". The check itself is correct.\n- **Independent-check map.** It covers PR2315, PR2286, PR2359, PR2402, PR2406, PR2442, PR2446, PR2453, PR2466 and PR2472, each with its scope qualifiers. **PR2436, PR2462 and PR2474, the top three claims, have no independent check yet.**\n\n### Reproduce\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-claim-lineage-ledger/ledger.py --fetch\n# PASS_T74_CLAIM_LEDGER prs=16 statements=95 (body 32, README 63) consistent=84 (ambiguous 2) flagged=2288r6,2302b2,2302r6,2312r8,2374b3,2374r5,2435b2,2435r1,2435r4,2447r1,2474r1 gates=82\n```\nThe command needs only the standard library. What it checks:\n- every claim file, README and release script against its git blob, and the claim files also against sha256;\n- every README quote against the README at its pinned head;\n- that the gate parse accounts for every gate line;\n- 315 negative controls, all rejected: perturbed numbers, wrong targets, altered quotes, wrong pins and synthetic gates. These run through the same functions as the real check.\n- 11 positive controls: each suggested correction must be consistent.\n\nThe optional `--live` mode checks pinned heads, body hashes and body quotes against GitHub. It returned `live_drift=0` at the snapshot; any drift exits with status 3.\n\n### Scope\n- The package checks text and gates only. No \u03ba, outer ledger or construction is re-derived.\n- The transcription coverage and its exclusions are listed in the README. Two adversarial review rounds found ten statements, one PR (PR2281) and one gate shape that the first sweeps missed.\n- Base: main `0fdd7d82d`. Everything ran on CPython 3.14.4. The registered Python 3.12 replay was not run. Package metadata check: `PASS_PACKAGE_METADATA_AND_PINS`; research unit tests pass.\n- Overlap: no earlier report or correction of these numbers was found in PR comments, PR searches or Discussions.\n\nPrepared by Sagar Thakrar with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5), including adversarial AI reviewers; no independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
